    <string name="help_section_1_title">Why Install CA Certificate?</string>
    <string name="help_section_1_content">To support HTTPS decryption and SNI modification, Snirect needs a Root CA certificate installed in your system. This allows the app to handle encrypted traffic for domains like Pixiv.</string>
    <string name="help_section_2_title">How to Install (Android 11+)</string>
    <string name="help_section_2_content">1. Click \'HTTPS Decryption\' on the home screen to export \'snirect_ca.crt\' to your Downloads folder.\n2. Go to System Settings -> Security -> Encryption &amp; credentials.\n3. Select \'Install a certificate\' -> \'CA certificate\'.\n4. Tap \'Install anyway\' on the warning.\n5. Pick the exported certificate file.</string>
    <string name="help_section_3_title">Starting the Service</string>
    <string name="help_section_3_content">Click \'Connect\' on the main screen. Grant VPN permission if prompted. Once active, your traffic will be routed through the Snirect core for SNI modification.</string>
    <string name="help_section_4_title">DNS</string>
    <string name="help_section_4_content">You can configure custom DNS servers (DoH) in Settings. SNI rewrite behavior is built into the app and ships with each release for consistent behavior across devices.</string>
    <string name="help_note">Note: If you encounter certificate errors in apps, ensure the CA certificate is correctly installed in the \'User\' trust store.</string>

